		}
	}
	\end{tikzpicture}

	\end{document}
	```

Replace `<FEN>` with your actual FEN notation and the code will generate a LaTeX output with the corresponding chessboard and pieces in their proper positions.

This code assumes that FEN notation follows the standard format, with pieces separated by slashes ('/') and rows separated by newlines. The `square` and `squarepiece` styles are defined as:

